title The projection refreshed on the cadence lap, and the push left at the gate
prompt Autonomous loop -- roster cold first, Standfast on reds, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota row N mod 5, condense ITINERARY and refill Now, send each finished increment, seed cadence on the closing lap
think Commit count reached 3425, so this is the lap the council rota closes its cycle -- 3425 mod 5 = 0 -- and the seed cadence falls due.
think The cadence grant and custody gate %1 point opposite ways on the same line, and ITINERARY settles it for itself rather than leaving it to the lap: the projection and its four gates are agent-doable, the force-push is Keaton's hand, and an autonomous lap surfaces that rather than reading the grant in its own favour. Precedents 20260823.142302 and 20260824.
think So I ran the half that is mine. sow_project.sh copied 7,038 files, scrubbed 1,080 and withheld 122 -- up from 6,961 and 1,066 at the last reading, which is five rounds of new work reaching the projection.
obs All four gates hold on the fresh projection, each read alone: IDENT_CLEAN from the leak scan, NO_PERSONAL from sow_witness, GREEN from seed_link_witness, and the projection itself SOW_OK. The card's reading was fifteen days stale in its counts and is measured now.
obs The force-push is left where it belongs. One line ships it -- bash ~/grain/publish-seed.sh -- and it waits on Keaton's word.
obs Own red, caught by the tooling and repaired without a force-push. I chained the ITINERARY nib sed and a `git commit --amend` behind the commit in one shell line, and the commit-msg hook refused the body for carrying two mechanism words where three are wanted. The amend fired anyway, on the commit BEFORE it -- the docs round already pushed as c21e4633b5 -- swallowing this lap's three files into a published commit and making the push a non-fast-forward.
obs The remotes were the record that saved it: they still held c21e4633b5, so `git reset --soft` back to it left this lap's work staged and cost nothing. No force-push, no history rewrite, no reclone for anyone.
obs What it taught, and it is the same shape as the mechanism-sentence law itself: a refusal is only a refusal if what follows it stops. `cmd && amend` would have stopped; `cmd; sed; amend` does not, and I wrote the second because the first four rounds had all succeeded. A step that rewrites a published commit belongs on its own line, after a verdict has been read by eyes.
loom seed copied=7038 scrubbed=1080 withheld=122 leak=IDENT_CLEAN sow=NO_PERSONAL seed_link=GREEN
file construction/ITINERARY.md the seed cadence reading refreshed from a projection run this minute
recommend check-in (Keaton) the seed force-push is the one door open and it is a custody gate -- say ship the seed and bash ~/grain/publish-seed.sh carries it; everything else on the card is agent-doable and the next crux is the fourth microkernel rung, the address space
